                "word": "sabretache",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3176d6ff-1070-4267-90c4-b72a6244f65c",
                        "entry_id": "f92fa9d3-591f-3aa5-a21a-b40cc4ef7678",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sabretaches"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4753cc7c-bd3d-3dbb-a052-2bc3ebed2777",
                        "entry_id": "f92fa9d3-591f-3aa5-a21a-b40cc4ef7678",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A leather pocket or pouch worn hanging from a cavalry officer’s belt."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e127afb-9e42-425c-83a2-adbb9debfb98",
                                "sense_id": "4753cc7c-bd3d-3dbb-a052-2bc3ebed2777",
                                "text": "There were five buttons blown off my dress jacket; the slings of my sabretache were cut off, but my sword belts were not touched."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f624f8c3-206d-4f03-997c-ffd7a03959bb",
                                "sense_id": "4753cc7c-bd3d-3dbb-a052-2bc3ebed2777",
                                "text": "1896, Letter from Winston Churchill, on Army duty in India, to his mother\nTwo years in Europe—with a campaign thrown in—would I think qualify me to be allowed to beat my sword into a paper cutter & my sabretache into an election address."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df59206e-085d-4cd1-afdd-d79cc8781759",
                                "sense_id": "4753cc7c-bd3d-3dbb-a052-2bc3ebed2777",
                                "text": "A hand-stitched black sabretache rested on the chair beside her, together with a wide cartwheel hat of gold straw, its crown encircled by a thin black velvet ribbon which tied at the back in a short bow."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "55c5081b-eaa3-43c6-9680-8d7d25f736db",
                        "source_entry_id": "f92fa9d3-591f-3aa5-a21a-b40cc4ef7678",
                        "source_sense_id": "4753cc7c-bd3d-3dbb-a052-2bc3ebed2777",
                        "source_sense_description": "hanging cavalry pouch",
                        "target_lang_word": "sabretache",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sabretache",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea1c88db-f9e2-3c4c-a478-0807ef0ff15c",
                                        "entry_id": "8aaa687f-606d-3f36-8d21-8c7c131da1b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de sac plat, suspendu par des courroies entre le fourreau du sabre et l'extérieur du jarret gauche d’un cavalier, pour amortir les battements pendant la marche, et qui lui servait en plus de poche, notamment pour le courrier. Il était traditionnellement fait en cuir noir à l'extérieur et en basane à l'intérieur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "491c725e-1b28-49bd-982c-e555a17b3824",
                                                "sense_id": "ea1c88db-f9e2-3c4c-a478-0807ef0ff15c",
                                                "text": "Ceci n’est pas une Scène de la Vie Militaire, où il serait tenu de ne pas mettre des sabretaches à des fantassins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24b1ddfd-866b-4adf-bce4-7f9b0b22d577",
                                                "sense_id": "ea1c88db-f9e2-3c4c-a478-0807ef0ff15c",
                                                "text": "Le repas fini, la table enlevée, on ouvrait un vieux piano qui dormait là depuis vingt ans et l’on se mettait à chanter des airs de France ; ou bien, sur une Lauterbach quelconque, un jeune Werther à sabretache faisait faire un tour de valse à Mlle Schontz."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a790dae6-3f07-4a06-b1c7-bd0ee9220255",
                                                "sense_id": "ea1c88db-f9e2-3c4c-a478-0807ef0ff15c",
                                                "text": "— Cré nom d’une sabretache ! C’est que cette hystérique finira par vous épouser malgré vous, je la connais."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7aebecb-eb77-46d4-960b-ba5b6c2a4950",
                        "source_entry_id": "f92fa9d3-591f-3aa5-a21a-b40cc4ef7678",
